From 62bbeef74b5f26ede8dbd7c3fa8b5bb762bfff58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 15:57:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0112 -- native Gravis Ultrasound (GF1) audio
 backend

Campaign 3. A native GF1 wavetable audio backend (new
src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_gus.c) driven OUT-OF-BAND, exactly like the shipped
AdLib/OPL path (SDL/0110's PIT/OPL exports). It is NOT an SDL streaming audio
device: no audio bootstrap, no SDL audio device opened, no SDL3_mixer PCM sink,
no SDL_INIT_AUDIO involvement. The engine brings the card up via
SDL_DOSGusInit() (mirroring the AdLib SDL_DOSOpl2Detect + pump start), then
uploads sample bytes into the card's on-board DRAM and commands GF1 hardware
voices through the exports in SDL3/SDL_dosgus.h. The GF1 mixes up to N voices
in hardware straight to its DAC; the host CPU does allocation + event dispatch
only.

Why DOS needs this: a GUS-only machine cannot open SDL_INIT_AUDIO today, so it
had to boot AUDIO_OFF. The engine adds a `gus` boot-mode that omits
SDL_INIT_AUDIO (like `adlib`) and drives the GF1 purely through these exports.
The Sound Blaster path is wholly untouched (no audio bootstrap, no shared
audio-core edit), so it stays byte-identical.

FULLY GF1-IRQ-INDEPENDENT (real-HW finding): a PicoGUS plays poll-based MIDIDEMO
but is SILENT for IRQ-driven Doom -- it does not deliver the GF1 IRQ to
IRQ-driven software. So this driver hooks NO GF1 IRQ and enables none: no ISR;
reset reg 0x4C=0x03 (IRQ bit2 off); per-voice wave-end IRQ never set
(SDL_DOSGUS_IRQ is a no-op); voice-reap polls voice_active_mask (GF1
voice-stopped hw bit); the music clock is the external PIT pump.

DRAM UPLOAD is 64KB-CRASH-SAFE (#36 real-HW fix): the g2k iter hard-crashed
during the SFX upload because the 8237 DMA transfer crossed a 64KB ISA
physical-page boundary (the controller wraps the offset within the page ->
memory corruption -> page-fault; DOSBox doesn't enforce it so smoke passed).
Fix:
  - DEFAULT upload path = programmed-I/O poke -- the SAME mechanism as GF1
    detection's DRAM peek/poke (proven on the operator's PicoGUS, which sized
    1024KB DRAM that way) and immune to the 8237/64KB crash. Done in bounded
    cli/sti bursts so a large per-song .pat upload can't starve the PIT clock /
    cooperative scheduler.
  - DMA upload is OPT-IN (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_GUS_DMA_UPLOAD=1), 8-bit only, and
    SPLIT into <=32KB 64KB-page-safe chunks through one boundary-safe bounce
    buffer so no single 8237 transfer can cross a page. Promote to default once
    g2k-validated.
  - DRAM allocations are 16-byte aligned (GF1 DMA dest reg 0x42 = addr>>4).

Other Phase-0 scope:
- SDL_DOSGusInit/Shutdown: parse ULTRASND/ULTRADIR/VOICES hints via SDL_GetHint
  (never getenv), GF1 reset, DRAM peek/poke detect + 256K sizing, set active
  voices (reg 0x0E -> rate), DAC enable; SKIP_DETECTION bypass.
- Voice ops alloc/start/stop/freq/vol/pan. Driver owns all GF1 conversions
  (FC=hz*1024/rate; 8-bit addr split; 16-bit bank quirk; linear->4.8-log vol;
  0-255->4-bit pan). 28 voices (~22050 Hz) at Init.
- IRQ-SAFE voice pool: AllocVoice/StartVoice/StopVoice mutate the shared
  busy-list inside cli/sti -- the pool is driven from BOTH the main loop
  (Pixtone SFX) AND the IRQ-0 music pump, so a preempting note_on must not
  double-claim a slot.
- SDL_DOSGusResetDram(keep_bytes) rewinds the DRAM bump cursor preserving a low
  keep region (persistent SFX bank survives per-song .pat swaps).
- Hints SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_GUS_{ULTRASND,ULTRADIR,VOICES,SKIP_DETECTION,DIAG,
  DMA_UPLOAD} (DIAG + DMA_UPLOAD default-OFF).
- REQUIRED detect banner "audio: SDL/0112 GUS GF1 detect: present=...".

GF1 register indices cross-checked vs DOSBox-X gus.cpp + the GUS SDK; the
IRQ/DMA latch + a few conversions are ACCURATE-BUT-CONFIRM inline pending the
operator's g2k register pass. Validated by a clean libSDL3.a link: 12 exports,
no audio bootstrap, no PC-speaker contamination, no GF1 IRQ hook.

gus-5 (#41 the .pat-upload freeze + #40 quiesce, folded in):
- #41 ROOT (IOCHRDY poke-overrun): the per-byte PIO path re-selected the FULL
  GF1 DRAM address (0x43/0x44, ~5 outportb) before EVERY data byte poked to
  3X7 -- ~6 port ops/byte. On the operator's PicoGUS (RP2040) this floods the
  card's ISA command path; the 2nd .pat instrument upload of a song overruns it,
  the card asserts IOCHRDY, and the outportb stalls the ISA bus with unbounded
  wait states while the driver holds cli -> CPU freeze. (Earlier "a bounded PIO
  loop can't hang" reasoning was wrong: a single outportb is not guaranteed to
  return when the card holds IOCHRDY.)
- #41 FIX (gated): SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_GUS_PIO_AUTOINC=1 programs the DRAM address
  ONCE per upload and pokes 3X7 sequentially, letting the GF1 auto-advance its
  own DRAM pointer -- ~1 outportb/byte (~6x fewer). Default OFF (per-byte = the
  observe cell) until g2k confirms autoinc reaches gameplay, then flip to ON.
- OBSERVE diags (GUS_DIAG-gated): the upload-start log now includes the live
  hardware active_mask (H1 contention vs H2 overrun decider), and gus_upload_pio
  emits a byte-offset progress line every ~1KB (last line before a freeze pins
  where the ISA bus wedged).
- #40 SDL_DOSGusStopAllVoices(): stops + frees every voice in one cli/sti pass
  (song-boundary quiesce; engine calls it at .pat residency swaps, never
  per-SFX). This is the 12th export.
- Test-tone (TESTTONE=1) now plays SYNCHRONOUSLY then EXPLICITLY StopVoice-frees
  voice 0 before Init returns -- no reliance on GF1 wave-end auto-stop, nothing
  lingering into gameplay; doubles as a #40 quiesce probe.
- "device up" banner gains upload=pio[+autoinc] to witness the active cell.
- New hint documented in docs/internal/BOOT.md.

gus-6 (#42 the post-upload first-note freeze -- the real music blocker):
- ROOT (code-confirmed): gus_encode_addr encoded the GF1 16-bit DRAM address
  with the READ-side transform (a = (a & 0xC0000) | ((a & 0x1FFFF) << 1)) -- the
  inverse of what a driver needs. The hardware then applies its own <<1 on read,
  so a 16-bit voice fetched from ~4*A (the wrong DRAM region: other instruments
  / un-uploaded garbage). All these .pat are 16-bit, so EVERY music voice
  mis-fetched. The PicoGUS mis-fetch then asserted IOCHRDY on the next card I/O
  -> CPU freeze right after on_song_start (no game-loop flips, no voice line).
  gus-2 never hit it (the old freq bug left voices near-DC, never fetching);
  #39 "in-tune" was an fc-value log check, not an ear check; DOSBox smoke never
  audibly plays a 16-bit voice -- so this path had never played on anything.
- FIX (one line): canonical GUS_16BIT_ADDR encode -- shift the in-bank offset
  RIGHT: a = (a & 0xC0000) | ((a >> 1) & 0x1FFFF). Round-trip is now exact
  (hw read-back == A). The 0x1FFFF mask is complete with >>1 (A spans 0..0x3FFFF
  in a 256K bank -> A>>1 spans 0..0x1FFFF, no bits dropped). Ref: Gravis SDK /
  Linux gus_wave.c; cross-checked vs DOSBox-X gus.cpp read xform.
- CONFIRM diag (GUS_DIAG): the per-voice START log reconstructs the programmed
  integer address from the actual encoded MSW|LSW, applies the GF1 read xform,
  and prints hw_fetch=0x... (==start? N) -- 1 proves the fetch lands on the
  uploaded address.
- A/B fallback hint SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_GUS_FORCE_8BIT_ADDR=1 (default OFF): forces
  8-bit voice addressing to isolate the 16-bit path if the encode fix does not
  fully clear the wedge. Diagnostic only.

gus-7 (#39 the post-#42 SILENCE: diagnostic bundle, IRQ-safe):

Static analysis exonerated the SDL voice path (DAC two-step 0x4C 0x00->0x01->0x03,
mix-ctrl line-out 0x08 bit1=0 active-low, gus_w8 high-byte placement, logvol<<4
into bits[15:4]) and DISPROVED the ramp-gating theory (DOSBox-X + DOSBox-staging:
a stopped ramp with non-zero static 0x09 IS audible -- ramp does not gate output).
So the silence needs RUNTIME values, but H5 blocked the diag. This bundle gets the
data:
- IRQ-SAFE voice-diag ring (the H5 fix): SetVoiceFreq/Vol + StartVoice run in the
  note_on PIT-IRQ, where doskutsu_dbg_log (fprintf+fsync) deadlocks via libc
  reentrancy (confirmed H5 -- GUS_DIAG=1 hung). The ops now ENQUEUE fixed records
  (FREQ hz/fc, VOL in/reg, START addr/ctrl) into a static ring INSIDE their
  existing cli (memory-only, no I/O); a MAIN-LOOP-only flush (GetState per-frame
  poll gated by an entry interrupt-flag check + a guaranteed flush at each
  on_song_start UploadSample) drains them. GUS_DIAG=1 is now runnable on g2k.
- POST-GO voice-status READ-BACK: StartVoice reads voice-control 0x80 (twice, GF1
  latch quirk) right after GO and enqueues RBACK status -- stopped=1 means the GF1
  did NOT run the voice (the decisive silence datum).
- FORCE_MAXVOL probe (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_GUS_FORCE_MAXVOL=1, default OFF): forces
  0x09=0xFFF0 in SetVoiceVol + StartVoice. A/B: audible -> the bug is the volume
  VALUE (engine low/zero vol or conversion); still silent -> volume path
  exonerated, deeper voice-run/DAC/PicoGUS cause (the ring + RBACK pin it).
- device-up banner gains " maxvol=ON"; new hint documented in BOOT.md.
No new export (still 12). The gus-6 hw_fetch START diag (also IRQ-context) is
replaced by the ring -- the >>1 encode is already confirmed.

gus-16 (#39 dead-zone PERMANENT FIX -- default voices 28 -> 14):

Root cause CONFIRMED on g2k (wave-gus16, same binary, A/B): the PicoGUS
PCM510xA DAC is dead-silent at EXACTLY 22.05kHz (~10% of cards; the reason
pgusinit ships /gus44k). Our GUS_DEF_VOICES=28 set the GF1 output rate to
617400/28 = 22050Hz -> the dead zone -> total silence. With GUS_VOICES=14
(617400/14 = 44100Hz) the SAME binary is audible + playable + save/load OK;
28 voices is silent. There is NO pitch/rate bug -- g_gus_rate is recomputed
from g_gus_voices, so 14 voices plays in tune at 44100Hz (highest quality).
The four prior register-gate fixes (double-write, vol-ramp, 0x4C=0x07,
FULLCANON) are REFUTED by this finding; they stay default-ON as background
correctness but none fixed #39.

The fix: GUS_DEF_VOICES 28 -> 14 (one line). 44100Hz is the highest-quality
GF1 point and clears the only DAC dead point. The SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_GUS_VOICES
hint still overrides for A/B, so no new killswitch is needed. Trade-off:
14-voice polyphony vs 28 -- the operator's 14-voice Organya had no dropped
notes, so 14 is the chosen default; a future trip could A/B a mid count
(24 -> 25725Hz, still clears the dead zone) if dense songs ever drop notes.
The g_gus_rate static initializer 22050 -> 44100 for consistency (cosmetic;
always recomputed before use). BOOT.md GUS_VOICES + AUDIO_BACKEND=gus entries
updated. Why DOS needs this: a no-SB DOS box on a PicoGUS /mode gus otherwise
boots to a silent default.

